# R3sults User Authentication API

**Base URL:** `DOMAIN_NAME from the env file/api/auth`

## Overview

JWT-based auth with **access + refresh tokens**. Supports four authentication methods:
- Phone + Password (register/login)
- Google Sign-In (OAuth ID token)
- Apple Sign-In (identity token)
- Phone OTP (passwordless)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> All tokens are signed with `JWT_SECRET`. Access tokens expire in **30 days** (configurable via `JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRY`), refresh tokens in **60 days** (`JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRY`).

---

## Environment Variables

| Variable | Required | Description |
|----------|----------|-------------|
| `JWT_SECRET` | ✅ | Secret for signing JWTs |
| `JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRY` | ❌ | Access token expiry (default: `30d`) |
| `JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRY` | ❌ | Refresh token expiry (default: `60d`) |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | For Google auth | Google OAuth Web client ID |
| `GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID` | For Google auth | Google OAuth iOS client ID |
| `GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID` | For Google auth | Google OAuth Android client ID |
| `TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID` | For SMS OTP | Twilio account SID |
| `TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN` | For SMS OTP | Twilio auth token |
| `TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER` | For SMS OTP | Twilio sender number |

---

## Authentication Header

All authenticated endpoints require:

```
Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>
```

---

## Endpoints

### 1. Register (Phone + Password)

```
POST /auth/register
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "password": "min6chars",
  "fullName": "John Doe",
  "email": "optional@email.com",
  "username": "optional_username"
}
```

**Response (201):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Registration successful. OTP sent for verification.",
  "data": {
    "userId": "cuid_xxx",
    "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
  }
}
```

> [!NOTE]
> After registration, the user must verify their phone via the **Verify OTP** endpoint to receive tokens.

---

### 2. Login (Phone + Password)

```
POST /auth/login
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "password": "your_password"
}
```

**Response (200):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "Login successful",
  "data": {
    "user": { "id": "...", "fullName": "...", "role": "MEMBER", ... },
    "accessToken": "eyJhbG...",
    "refreshToken": "eyJhbG..."
  }
}
```

**Errors:** `401` Invalid credentials · `403` Account deactivated

---

### 3. Google Sign-In

```
POST /auth/google
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "idToken": "google_id_token_from_client_sdk"
}
```

**Response (200):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "user": { ... },
    "needsPhoneUpdate": true,
    "accessToken": "eyJhbG...",
    "refreshToken": "eyJhbG..."
  }
}
```

> [!TIP]
> **For web:** Use the Google Identity Services library to get the `idToken`. The backend validates against `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`, `GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID`, and `GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID` — add your web client ID to `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`.
>
> If `needsPhoneUpdate` is `true`, prompt the user to add their phone number via `POST /auth/update-phone`.

---

### 4. Apple Sign-In

```
POST /auth/apple
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "identityToken": "apple_identity_token",
  "user": {
    "fullName": { "givenName": "John", "familyName": "Doe" }
  }
}
```

**Response (200):** Same shape as Google Sign-In.

> [!NOTE]
> Apple only provides the user's name on **first sign-in**. After that, `user.fullName` will be `null`.

---

### 5. Send OTP (Passwordless)

```
POST /auth/phone/send-otp
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}
```

**Response (200):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "OTP sent successfully",
  "data": { "phoneNumber": "+1234567890", "expiresIn": 300 }
}
```

Creates a new user if the phone number doesn't exist. OTP expires in **5 minutes**.

---

### 6. Verify OTP

```
POST /auth/phone/verify-otp
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "otp": "123456"
}
```

**Response (200):** Returns `user`, `accessToken`, [refreshToken](file:///Users/ayushmac/CodeProjects/R3sults/src/services/api.ts#385-392) (same shape as Login).

**Errors:** `400` Invalid/expired OTP · `429` Too many attempts (max 5)

---

### 7. Forgot Password

```
POST /auth/forgot-password
```

**Body:**
```json
{ "phoneNumber": "+1234567890" }
```

**Response (200):** Always returns success (doesn't reveal if account exists).

---

### 8. Reset Password

```
POST /auth/reset-password
```

**Body:**
```json
{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "otp": "123456",
  "newPassword": "new_min_6_chars"
}
```

**Response (200):** `{ "success": true, "message": "Password reset successful. Please login again." }`

Invalidates the current refresh token — user must login again.

---

### 9. Refresh Token

```
POST /auth/refresh-token
```

**Body:**
```json
{ "refreshToken": "eyJhbG..." }
```

**Response (200):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "accessToken": "new_access_token",
    "refreshToken": "new_refresh_token"
  }
}
```

> [!CAUTION]
> Refresh tokens are **single-use**. The old refresh token is invalidated after each refresh. Store the new one.

---

### 10. Get Current User 🔒

```
GET /auth/me
```

**Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`

**Response (200):**
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": { "user": { "id": "...", "fullName": "...", ... } }
}
```

---

### 11. Update Phone 🔒

```
POST /auth/update-phone
```

**Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`

**Body:**
```json
{ "phoneNumber": "+9876543210" }
```

Sends an OTP to the new number. Use **Verify OTP** to confirm.

---

### 12. Logout 🔒

```
POST /auth/logout
```

**Headers:** `Authorization: Bearer <accessToken>`

Invalidates the refresh token server-side.

---

## JWT Token Payload

### Access Token
```json
{
  "id": "user_cuid",
  "role": "MEMBER",
  "type": "user",
  "iat": 1709000000,
  "exp": 1711592000
}
```

### Refresh Token
```json
{
  "id": "user_cuid",
  "type": "user",
  "iat": 1709000000,
  "exp": 1714184000
}
```

---

## Web Integration Quick Start

```javascript
// 1. Login
const res = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/auth/login`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ phoneNumber: '+1234567890', password: 'secret' }),
});
const { data } = await res.json();
localStorage.setItem('accessToken', data.accessToken);
localStorage.setItem('refreshToken', data.refreshToken);

// 2. Authenticated request
const profile = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/auth/me`, {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${localStorage.getItem('accessToken')}` },
});

// 3. Refresh when expired (401)
const refresh = await fetch(`${API_BASE}/api/auth/refresh-token`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ refreshToken: localStorage.getItem('refreshToken') }),
});
const tokens = await refresh.json();
localStorage.setItem('accessToken', tokens.data.accessToken);
localStorage.setItem('refreshToken', tokens.data.refreshToken);
```

> [!TIP]
> For Google Sign-In on web, use `@react-oauth/google` or the Google Identity Services JS SDK. Pass the `credential` (ID token) to `POST /auth/google`.

